  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Cormac is riding a ferris wheel. The height $H$ in metres of his seat above the ground after $t$ minutes can be modelled by the function:\n$$H(t)=b+a\\cos(nt).$$\nThe graph of $H(t)$ for the duration of the ride is shown below.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q2-graph",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"curveBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"function curve distinguished from axes and guides\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 23, p23-q2-graph\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.35cm,y=0.38cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\draw[->,black,line width=0.5pt] (0,0)--(4.35,0) node[right] {$t$};\n\\draw[->,black,line width=0.5pt] (0,0)--(0,11) node[above] {$H(t)$};\n\\foreach \\h in {2,6,10}{\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (0,\\h)--(4,\\h);\\node[left] at (0,\\h) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\h$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\foreach \\t in {1,2,3,4}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\t,-0.15)--(\\t,0.15);\\node[below] at (\\t,0) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\t$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\draw[curveBlue,line width=0.8pt,domain=0:4,samples=161] plot (\\x,{6-4*cos(180*\\x)});\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 70,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 23,
          "sourceRegion": "Upper left column, above Question 2(a)",
          "description": "Cosine height graph with arrowed axes, four labelled time ticks and dashed horizontal guides at heights 2, 6 and 10.",
          "mathematics": "Domain 0≤t≤4; H(t)=6−4cos(πt); minima (0,2), (2,2), (4,2); maxima (1,10), (3,10).",
          "answerVisibility": "Supplied graph remains visible in the question edition."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the values of $a$ and $b$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=-4,\\quad b=6$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}b&=\\frac{10+2}{2}\\\\b&=6\\\\|a|&=\\frac{10-2}{2}\\\\|a|&=4\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph starts at its minimum, so the cosine coefficient is negative. Hence $a=-4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the period of the function. Hence, calculate $n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Period $=2$ minutes; $n=\\pi$.",
          "worked": "Consecutive maxima occur at $t=1$ and $t=3$, so the period is $2$ minutes.\n$$\\begin{align*}2&=\\frac{2\\pi}{n}\\\\2n&=2\\pi\\\\n&=\\pi\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "How far above the ground is the seat after 20 seconds?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4\\text{ m}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}t&=\\frac{20}{60}=\\frac13\\text{ min}\\\\H\\left(\\frac13\\right)&=6-4\\cos\\left(\\frac\\pi3\\right)\\\\H\\left(\\frac13\\right)&=6-4\\left(\\frac12\\right)\\\\H\\left(\\frac13\\right)&=4\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "At what times (in minutes) is the seat 8 metres above the ground?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=\\frac23,\\ \\frac43,\\ \\frac83,\\ \\frac{10}3$ minutes.\n\nSolve $\\cos(\\pi t)=-\\frac12$ over the four-minute ride.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}6-4\\cos(\\pi t)&=8\\\\-4\\cos(\\pi t)&=2\\\\\\cos(\\pi t)&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nFor $0\\le t\\le4$, the angle satisfies $0\\le\\pi t\\le4\\pi$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\pi t&=\\frac{2\\pi}{3},\\ \\frac{4\\pi}{3},\\ \\frac{8\\pi}{3},\\ \\frac{10\\pi}{3}\\\\t&=\\frac23,\\ \\frac43,\\ \\frac83,\\ \\frac{10}3\\text{ min}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
